WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.020
- Last season,

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.720
we had Connie's Friday
Night Lights husband,

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:04.802
who I love as well,

00:00:04.802 --> 00:00:05.635
(Connie laughs)

00:00:05.635 --> 00:00:06.468
Kyle Chandler,

00:00:06.468 --> 00:00:09.000
and we had him on, and he told this story

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.130
about working with you, let's take a look.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.080
- Connie and I, when we'd
be working on the set,

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.210
'cause we'd improv every once in a while,

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.190
and I would also bring fights that my wife

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.200
and I would have that
were sort of unresolved,

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.960
and I would create them again on the show.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.240
- I mean, here's the thing.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.797
Just look at him.
- [Connie] He's so cute.

00:00:25.797 --> 00:00:26.630
Isn't he cute?

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:27.780
He's so cute.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.580
- I love that he said that he
would take things from home.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.250
Did you ever improvise with
things in your own life?

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.310
- Oh, well you know it's
hilarious that he said that,

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.533
because we did so much improvisation.

00:00:38.726 --> 00:00:40.020
- [Kelly] Which is why it was so great.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.580
- Well, and also,

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.720
I'll just say this,
even though this is not

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.873
answering your question,
but we'll get back to that.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.610
We played husband and wife.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:48.443
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:48.443 --> 00:00:52.650
- And he had, he has
such an amazing marriage.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:54.300
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.160
- They were so inspiring,

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.160
and I feel like he brought a lot of that

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.020
into the work that we were doing.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:01.853
- Wow.

00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:04.410
- And so it was really
wonderful 'cause it felt like,

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.300
it felt like he was really
sharing that with us.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.170
Not in a weird way.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.003
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.370
- But there's one thing that I think about

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.533
when we talk about improvising.

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.080
We had this scene once.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:16.980
I don't know if you remember it

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.960
or how much of a Friday
Night Lights head you are.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:19.920
- Saw every episode.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.610
- But there was a scene where our daughter

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:27.930
and Matt Saracen are watching
a movie on the couch,

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:31.830
and Kyle goes in and
he just like freaks out

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.210
and they have a blanket,

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:34.320
and he takes the blanket

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.153
away from them.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:35.153 --> 00:01:36.150
- He's like, you gotta get out of here.

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:36.983
And then,

00:01:36.983 --> 00:01:38.228
and I'm just.
- What's happening

00:01:38.228 --> 00:01:39.061
under that blanket?

00:01:39.061 --> 00:01:40.200
- Right, exactly, and
Tammy is just looking,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.640
I'm just looking at him like this.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.800
And I say, you're an idiot.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.160
And that for me was a
throwback to a show that I did

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.110
in the nineties called Spin City.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:50.820
- Love Spin City!
- [Connie] Spin City,

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.740
remember with Michael J. Fox?
- I love Spin City.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.600
- That was the first TV show I ever did.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.090
And we, as a term of endearment,

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:58.860
the actors on that show,

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.610
we'd always be like, you're an idiot.

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:02.790
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And so I brought that into,

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:05.250
that was my contribution
to Friday Night Lights.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.660
- One word, one third.
- You're welcome,

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:07.493
you're welcome.

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.000
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:09.930
- Calling him an idiot.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:11.250
- I love it.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.990
I love everything you do, I'm not kidding.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:13.950
I love Spin City.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:16.230
But my son is five and your son is 10.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.610
So what do I have to look forward to,

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.140
and what should I be scared about?

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:19.973
- Okay, okay.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.720
- 'Cause I already feel
like we're headed to the ER

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.070
like every day.

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.900
- Okay, well that's not gonna change.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.160
- Yeah, he's just wild.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.246
He wants to be Peter Pan, yeah.

00:02:28.246 --> 00:02:29.079
You can't fly.
- [Connie] Oh he wants

00:02:29.079 --> 00:02:29.912
to be Peter Pan?

00:02:29.912 --> 00:02:31.860
- Can't fly baby.
- Oh no.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.300
Oh dear, well let's keep trying.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:34.154
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- Oh, nope.

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:34.987
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:34.987 --> 00:02:37.890
Well, that's unfortunately
not gonna change,

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.930
I don't believe.
- Yeah, great, okay.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:40.763
Truth, I like it.

00:02:40.763 --> 00:02:41.596
- It is fun.

00:02:41.596 --> 00:02:43.803
Like this sort of 10 year old age,

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.100
you can tell that they're
really starting to

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:50.760
think for themselves

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.790
and have a sense of who
they are in the world,

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:56.163
and think about other people around them.

00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:00.840
It's a subtle shift,
but suddenly it's like,

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.180
oh I want to have a conversation with him.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.179
I want to hang with him.

00:03:04.179 --> 00:03:05.012
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:05.012 --> 00:03:05.845
- I want to hang with him,

00:03:05.845 --> 00:03:06.678
and have conversations with him,

00:03:06.678 --> 00:03:07.950
and know who he is.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:08.783
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:08.783 --> 00:03:10.800
- And he's so smart.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:11.900
Like he comes up with,

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.800
he can give directions
like nobody's business.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.600
He'll have observations about things

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.460
that I never even thought about before.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:21.480
- That's what I love about kids.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:22.920
- [Connie] Yeah, I know.
- Yeah.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.240
- And it just kind of gets better

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:25.440
and better that way, I think.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.600
So I'm just gonna tell myself that way

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.100
and it's gonna I'm sure
be that way all the way

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.390
through the teenage years.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.120
- Totally, you'll have no issues.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.300
- No, no, no, no.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.740
It's gonna be just like that.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.120
- So easy.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.560
So wait, when you were
living in Nashville,

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.110
what was your favorite place to hang out?

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.340
- Oh

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:42.173
gosh.

00:03:42.173 --> 00:03:44.250
- Mine was actually
Bluebird before it was like,

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:45.150
everybody knew about.
- [Connie] Really?

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.680
- Everybody in Nashville
knew, and country,

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.830
but I did love, anytime I
could see the Time Jumpers,

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:50.720
they played The Station Inn I think.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:51.720
- Oh yeah, totally.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.180
- And then I'd go to Bluebird Cafe.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:56.520
But it was before it blew up or whatever.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:57.592
Now everybody's there all the time.

00:03:57.592 --> 00:03:58.737
- [Connie] I know, I know.

00:03:58.737 --> 00:04:01.560
- But I love like all the,
you can see music everywhere.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.630
- The Bluebird is, I know,
well I love the Ryman.

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:04.560
- Oh my gosh.
- I would say the Ryman

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:05.670
is one of my favorite places.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:07.800
That feels like church to me.
- To hear a show is great.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:08.700
Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:10.500
And we got, you know, we were so lucky,

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.760
we got to shoot there so much.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:12.593
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- I'm sure you

00:04:12.593 --> 00:04:13.426
played there a bunch.

00:04:13.426 --> 00:04:14.259
- I have played there,

00:04:14.259 --> 00:04:15.420
but I'm telling you what,

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.800
the coolest show you got to be a part of

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.660
and do all these cool things in Nashville

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.632
that artists die to do.

00:04:20.632 --> 00:04:21.465
- I know.
- Yeah.

00:04:21.465 --> 00:04:23.250
- I know, it was really,

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:26.070
I will always look back at
that period of time for me

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:29.070
and just be like, I
cannot believe I got to

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:30.660
have that be part of my life.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.180
- Yeah and it's a fun little community.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:35.940
But do you still make music
like you did on the show?

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.320
I mean, once you start doing that

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:38.153
isn't it kind of a part of you?

00:04:38.153 --> 00:04:40.440
You don't find yourself
doing anything like that?

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:44.460
- I'm back to what's
prompted me to have the nerve

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.020
to say yes to Nashville
in the first place,

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:48.270
which is basically just
singing around the house.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.710
- Okay, but that's fun.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.210
- Yeah, it's fun, it's great.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:52.950
- Yeah.
- And singing with my kids,

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:54.900
singing with Yoby.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:56.280
He's now very musical.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:58.830
I really do believe 'cause
he grew up in Nashville.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:04:59.663
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:59.663 --> 00:05:02.400
- While I was doing that
show and he now loves music.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.406
- What a cool thing you've done for him.

00:05:04.406 --> 00:05:05.820
Growing up around that.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:06.840
- It's one of those things, I don't know,

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:09.039
nature, nurture is always
so hard to figure out.

00:05:09.039 --> 00:05:09.872
- See which one, yeah.

00:05:09.872 --> 00:05:12.570
- I don't know if maybe
it really did impact him

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:14.190
or maybe he was just always gonna be

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:16.470
destined to love music.
- Yeah.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:18.060
- So we sing together a lot.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.170
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.003
- And love to listen to music.

00:05:20.003 --> 00:05:22.110
- There is nothing sweeter
than singing with your kids

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:23.040
and hearing their little voice.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.120
- [Connie] Oh my gosh.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:25.680
- Like you could sing
for thousands of people

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:26.513
and they're singing along,

00:05:26.513 --> 00:05:27.969
but when it's your kids, you're like, ugh.

00:05:27.969 --> 00:05:28.802
- [Connie] Yeah.

00:05:28.802 --> 00:05:29.635
- I break in such a great way.

00:05:29.635 --> 00:05:30.468
- I know.

00:05:30.468 --> 00:05:31.987
- What do you all sing around the house?

00:05:31.987 --> 00:05:32.820
Do you have favorites?

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:33.653
- Well, he has a playlist.

00:05:33.653 --> 00:05:34.800
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:37.290
- That he started when he was like five.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:38.280
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:39.540
- Every time he'd hear a song,

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:40.950
he'd be like Mom put that on my playlist.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:44.640
And now that playlist is hours
and hours and hours long.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:45.473
- I love it.

00:05:45.473 --> 00:05:47.250
- And it's funny 'cause
it's really evolved.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:48.960
And now, let's see, what
are some of the ones?

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:50.400
Now he's really into BTS.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.080
Now he's introducing me to music.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:52.913
- Okay.

00:05:52.913 --> 00:05:54.600
My niece loves it.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.210
She's 14 and she loves BTS, all the K-pop.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:58.702
She's really into it.
- [Connie] Yeah, yeah.

00:05:58.702 --> 00:05:59.970
Okay, that's what that is?
- I'm like okay,

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:01.200
I get into it, I sing it at the house.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.880
I'm like cool, all right.
- Yeah.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.560
He also loves country music.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:06.030
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:07.890
- Which I'm sure was probably
the Nashville influence,

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:09.210
but he likes pretty much everything.

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.920
So it's like a little eclectic mix.

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:11.753
- [Kelly] That's cool.

00:06:11.753 --> 00:06:12.930
- And he'll listen to it every day.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.550
- Oh my God, the same song
over and over and over.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:15.636
- Yeah.

00:06:15.636 --> 00:06:16.500
Over and over and over again.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:17.670
Yes.
- Cool, we're hearing it

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:18.840
again, that's exciting.

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:19.673
- Okay.

00:06:19.673 --> 00:06:20.850
- I didn't get it the first 50 times

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.700
but now I've got the whole song down.

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.190
- I learned it, never knew
I wanted to know a BTS song,

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:27.683
but now I know all the words.

00:06:27.683 --> 00:06:28.516
- But now I can do the dance moves.

00:06:28.516 --> 00:06:29.910
- [Connie] Yes, yes.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:31.443
- I love that this was my dance move.

00:06:31.443 --> 00:06:32.820
(Connie laughing)

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:33.721
Such a mom at this point.
- [Connie] I feel like

00:06:33.721 --> 00:06:35.353
it's right for K-pop.

